# ☕ Coffee Shop Website

A simple and inviting coffee shop website built with **HTML**, **Tailwind CSS**, and **pure JavaScript** (no frameworks).

---

## ✨ Features

- **Responsive** design that works on mobile, tablet, and desktop.
- Eye-catching hero section.
- **Menu** section showcasing drinks and desserts.
- **About Us** and **Contact** sections.
- Responsive navbar with a mobile menu toggle.
- Lightweight interactions powered by vanilla JavaScript.

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| HTML5 | Page structure and content |
| Tailwind CSS | Styling and responsive design |
| JavaScript (Vanilla) | Interactivity and dynamic behavior |

## 📁 Project Structure

```
coffee-shop/
├── index.html        # Main page
├── css/
│   └── style.css     # Custom styles (if any)
├── js/
│   └── main.js       # JavaScript file
└── README.md
```

> Adjust the structure above to match your actual project files.

## 🚀 Getting Started

No dependencies or build tools are required:

1. **Clone the repository**
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/masterhackingalfa-star/Mern-Stack-Project-1.git
   ```
2. **Navigate to the project folder**
   ```bash
   cd coffee-shop
   ```
3. **Open `index.html`** in your browser.

You can also use the **Live Server** extension in VS Code for instant previews while editing.

## 🎨 A Note on Tailwind CSS

This project loads Tailwind via **CDN** for a quick and simple setup:

```html
<script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
```

> This approach is great for development and small projects. For production, it's recommended to use the Tailwind CLI to generate a minified, optimized CSS file.

## 🔧 Customization

- **Colors and fonts:** Edit the Tailwind configuration inside a `<script>` tag or in `tailwind.config.js`.
- **Menu:** Update drinks and prices directly in `index.html`.

